      "notes_text": "Note\r\n07.07.2025          16:07:23            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n07.07.2025          15:46:08            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\nFollowing solution from Lauren Koenig:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting:Issue Reported: Says remote box not being detected on a computer Equipment Type and Model: Elite/2.0 USB remote modu\r\nle Serial Number: 166498166498 Acquisition Software & Version: CDR DICOM 3.5 Issue in One or All Rooms: One at the moment Other Sens\r\nors work with working Remotes in Room(s) with Issue: No PC Name: TWL1-OP8 Schick Driver Version (Programs and features): 5.16.484.10\r\n925 Remote FW/FPGA Version: _Not detected_ Sensor FW Version: _Not detected_ If Remote Issue: YES - Seems so 2.0 or 3.0: Tried Diffe\r\nrent USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: YES - Tried different port and a different USB cable they had and same behavior\r\n 3.0 Remote: Tried on a 3.0 AND 2.0 USB port/cable clip connected: N/A If Sensor Issue, Replaced Elastomer: N/A If Sensor Issue, Tri\r\ned Different Sensor Cable: N/A If no response to radiation, confirmed Xray Head Functional: N/A Additional Troubleshooting Steps/Not\r\nes: Had them wiggle the USB cable between remote box and the computer and each time they did a Program Compatibility Assistant dialo\r\ngue box appeared stating that a driver cannot load on this device - Driver: SynergyUSBx64.sys - A security setting is preventing it\r\nfrom installing. Seems to happen every time it is plugged in or unplugged. Tried a different USB cable and port on the computer and\r\nsame thing. They didnt have a spare 2.0 box to try and plug in to test against. Device only shows up in dealer orders, doesnt show\r\n up in normal Sirona component finder or anywhere in PTS PART PTC PROCESSING RMA FOR: ELITE/2.0 USB Remote Module\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n01.07.2025          19:40:23             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting:Issue Reported: Says remote box not being detected on a computer Equipment Type and Model: Elite/2.0 USB remote modu\r\nle Serial Number: 166498166498 Acquisition Software & Version: CDR DICOM 3.5 Issue in One or All Rooms: One at the moment Other Sens\r\nors work with working Remotes in Room(s) with Issue: No PC Name: TWL1-OP8 Schick Driver Version (Programs and features): 5.16.484.10\r\n925 Remote FW/FPGA Version: _Not detected_ Sensor FW Version: _Not detected_ If Remote Issue: YES - Seems so 2.0 or 3.0: Tried Diffe\r\nrent USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: YES - Tried different port and a different USB cable they had and same behavior\r\n 3.0 Remote: Tried on a 3.0 AND 2.0 USB port/cable clip connected: N/A If Sensor Issue, Replaced Elastomer: N/A If Sensor Issue, Tri\r\ned Different Sensor Cable: N/A If no response to radiation, confirmed Xray Head Functional: N/A Additional Troubleshooting Steps/Not\r\nes: Had them wiggle the USB cable between remote box and the computer and each time they did a Program Compatibility Assistant dialo\r\ngue box appeared stating that a driver cannot load on this device - Driver: SynergyUSBx64.sys - A security setting is preventing it\r\nfrom installing. Seems to happen every time it is plugged in or unplugged. Tried a different USB cable and port on the computer and\r\nsame thing. They didnt have a spare 2.0 box to try and plug in to test against. Device only shows up in dealer orders, doesnt show\r\n up in normal Sirona component finder or anywhere in PTS PART PTC PROCESSING RMA FOR: ELITE/2.0 USB Remote Module\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem 