      "description_text": "spare part: ptc proc rma 2038789/ no inf",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n07.07.2025          16:13:01            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n07.07.2025          15:30:52            Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN)\r\n\r\nFurther Action\r\n------------------\r\nSiro Force Part Request\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n07.07.2025          15:28:41            Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN)\r\n\r\nReplacing the interface\r\n\r\nPart request\r\n\r\n100008290 SCHICK 3.0 USB INTERFACE, RMA\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n01.07.2025          22:17:35             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nDetails: Yesterday we have our digital xrays hooked up. all seem to be running well besides one. now today 4 of them are having 4 d\r\nifferent issues\r\n\r\n\r\nOpti1-PC1\r\nsensor does not pull up on this box. box shows up in AE Usb interface. But the sensor does not just fail\r\ns to acquire it.\r\ntook sensor from OPTI1 and moved to Hygiene 10.  Sensor worked.\r\ntook box from this room and plugged into other com\r\nputers and it did not work\r\nasked office to try USB port on back of computer for the box......\r\n\r\n\r\nHgien10\r\nthis box needed a firmware u\r\npdate. but was able to take an xray with the sensor from Opti1 box sn: 2038789\r\n\r\nHygiene 11\r\nthis computer we tried the same sensor(op\r\nt1) sensor and it worked. Asked office to take badbox into this room and plug it in. Box still didnt work.\r\n\r\n782014713\r\nsvjey4c9\r\n\r\nHy\r\ngiene 12.\r\nfirmware update on box: this one worked the computer light just wasnt green. opened eaglesoft and it worked.\r\n\r\n\r\nIssue Repo\r\nrted: Wont pick up on sensor\r\n\r\nEquipment Type and Model: Schick USB interface  3.0\r\n\r\nSerial Number: 2038789\r\n\r\nAcquisition Software & V\r\nersion: Patterson Eaglesoft\r\n\r\nIssue in One or All Rooms: 1 room. but box stays in room\r\n\r\nOther Sensors work with working Remotes in R\r\noom(s) with Issue: NO\r\n\r\nPC Name: OPT1-PC1\r\n\r\nSchick Driver Version (Programs and features): AE USB interface\r\n\r\nRemote FW/FPGA Version: 1\r\n.5.140 Sensor FW Version: NA\r\n\r\nIf Remote Issue: YES\r\n\r\n2.0 or 3.0: Tried Different USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: Y\r\n\r\n3\r\n.0 Remote: Tried on a 3.0 AND 2.0 USB port/cable clip connected: Y\r\n\r\nIf Sensor Issue, Replaced Elastomer:\r\n\r\nIf Sensor Issue, Tried Dif\r\nferent Sensor Cable:\r\n\r\nIf no response to radiation, confirmed Xray Head Functional:\r\n\r\nAdditional Troubleshooting Steps/Notes:\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n01.07.2025          22:17:34             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nDetails: Yesterday we have our digital xrays hooked up. all seem to be running well besides one. now today 4 of them are having 4 d\r\nifferent issues\r\n\r\n\r\nOpti1-PC1\r\nsensor does not pull up on this box. box shows up in AE Usb interface. But the sensor does not just fail\r\ns to acquire it.\r\ntook sensor from OPTI1 and moved to Hygiene 10.  Sensor worked.\r\ntook box from this room and plugged into other com\r\nputers and it did not work\r\nasked office to try USB port on back of computer for the box......\r\n\r\n\r\nHgien10\r\nthis box needed a firmware u\r\npdate. but was able to take an xray with the sensor from Opti1 box sn: 2038789\r\n\r\nHygiene 11\r\nthis computer we tried the same sensor(op\r\nt1) sensor and it worked. Asked office to take badbox into this room and plug it in. Box still didnt work.\r\n\r\n782014713\r\nsvjey4c9\r\n\r\nHy\r\ngiene 12.\r\nfirmware update on box: this one worked the computer light just wasnt green. opened eaglesoft and it worked.\r\n\r\n\r\nIssue Repo\r\nrted: Wont pick up on sensor\r\n\r\nEquipment Type and Model: Schick USB interface  3.0\r\n\r\nSerial Number: 2038789\r\n\r\nAcquisition Software & V\r\nersion: Patterson Eaglesoft\r\n\r\nIssue in One or All Rooms: 1 room. but box stays in room\r\n\r\nOther Sensors work with working Remotes in R\r\noom(s) with Issue: NO\r\n\r\nPC Name: OPT1-PC1\r\n\r\nSchick Driver Version (Programs and features): AE USB interface\r\n\r\nRemote FW/FPGA Version: 1\r\n.5.140 Sensor FW Version: NA\r\n\r\nIf Remote Issue: YES\r\n\r\n2.0 or 3.0: Tried Different USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: Y\r\n\r\n3\r\n.0 Remote: Tried on a 3.0 AND 2.0 USB port/cable clip connected: Y\r\n\r\nIf Sensor Issue, Replaced Elastomer:\r\n\r\nIf Sensor Issue, Tried Dif\r\nferent Sensor Cable:\r\n\r\nIf no response to radiation, confirmed Xray Head Functional:\r\n\r\nAdditional Troubleshooting Steps/Notes:\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n01.07.2025          22:17:34             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
