      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "image quality",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n23.07.2025          17:28:04            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/23/2025 11:27:12 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Grace Rudersdorf\r\nCallers Phone Number: 3032371553\r\nCallers Role: Dr\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Follw up\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: Not available left vm with Ann front desk\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n17.07.2025          20:22:46            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/17/2025 2:20:48 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Grace Rudersdorf\r\nCallers Phone Number: 3032371553\r\nCallers Role: Dr\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Follow up\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: No answer left VM\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n15.07.2025          23:50:23            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/15/2025 5:49:26 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Timothy Plakon\r\nCallers Phone Number: 4072213434\r\nCallers Role:  Sales\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Follow up\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: Customer still having issues will follow up with the customer.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n12.07.2025          00:29:17            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/11/2025 4:30:25 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Mark Morey\r\nCallers Phone Number: 720-827-7574\r\nCallers Role: Patterson tech\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nI remoted into OP6 found 5.16 driver with 2808 patch also IOSS 3.2 installed. I uninstalled wiped IOSS 3.2 and C++, 5.16 and 2808 patch and reinstalled IOSS 3.2 and C++2005 to 2015-2022 .\r\nI remoted into OP7 found 5.16 driver with 2808 patch also IOSS 3.2 installed. I uninstalled wiped IOSS 3.2 and C++, 5.16 and 2808 patch and reinstalled IOSS 3.2 and C++2005 to 2015-2022 .\r\nI remoted into OP4 found 5.16 driver with 2808 patch, Sidexis, Schick integration also IOSS 3.2 installed. I uninstalled wiped Sidexis, IOSS 3.2 and C++, 5.16 and 2808 patch and reinstalled IOSS 3.2 and C++2005 to 2015-2022 .\r\nI remoted into OP2 integration missing from OP2 ran registry key to readd integration. Selected schick sesnor as default isse resolved.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\nFull mouth series taken on all ops tested successful.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n03.07.2025          22:31:56            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/03/2025 12:31:31 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Dr. Grace E. Rudersdorf,\r\nCallers Phone Number: 4029682567.\r\nCallers Role: Doctor\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Sensors disconnecting\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: I remoted into OP1 and 5.16 driver was found along with 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I removed all wiped folders and reinstalled only IOSS 3.2. Found corrupted C++ removed all reinstalled clean. Also found a work around for 2.0 remotes to work in Eaglesoft 24.\r\nSidexis 2.63 was found still to be installed. I uninstalled and wiped. Test shot successful but then stop working.\r\n\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP1 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files. A test shot was initially successful however, it stopped functioning afterward. Further evaluation may be needed if the issue persists.\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP2 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files.\r\n\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP3 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files. A test shot was attempted but sensor stop being detected.\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up: I recommend replacing the USB interface.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n02.07.2025          13:44:25            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis ticket is a continuation of a previous ticket for the same ongoing issue.  For this reason, it will be classified as an inquiry and therefore not counted as a complaint because it was already previously counted and trended at our Product Surveillance Meeting.  This ticket references the original ticket (for linkage) and will provide any additional information/actions taken on this issue.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n02.07.2025          13:44:24            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\nProblem Description\r\n01.07.2025          23:59:43            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\nContinuation of 1251558\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n01.07.2025          23:59:43            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/01/2025 5:59:09 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty:\r\nDealer on-site:\r\nBillable: N\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n90 Day Expiration Date: 09/29/2025\r\n\r\nRemote Access:\r\nSidexis Version:\r\nServer Location:\r\nPDATA Remote Location:\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable):\r\nPractice Management:\r\nWorkstation(s):\r\nScout Check:\r\n\r\nFirmware:\r\nPlug-in Version:\r\nExposure Count:\r\nUnit IP Address:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: I reached out and left my email to schedule for some troubleshooting.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________",
