      "ticket_id": "8001255465",
      "created_at": "2025-07-03",
      "record_type_group": "COMPLAINT",
      "region": "US",
      "language": "en",
      "category_level_2": "Schick 33 with AE USB",
      "category_level_3": "SW-Installation",
      "category_level_4": "Update / Installation support",
      "firmware": "1.5.140",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "usb issues",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n07.07.2025          14:30:09            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n03.07.2025          23:03:02            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/03/2025 4:04:58 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: unknown\r\nDealer on-site: No\r\nBillable: No  - Canadian Customer\r\nBilling Accepted: N/A\r\nBilling Approved By: N/A\r\n\r\nRemote Access: Yes\r\nSidexis Version: N/A\r\nServer Location: N/A\r\nPDATA Remote Location: N/A\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable): N/A\r\nPractice Management: Tracker\r\nWorkstation(s): OP2\r\nScout Check: Yes\r\n\r\nFirmware: USB v. 1.5.140 / Sensor v. 3.4\r\nPlug-in Version: IOSS 3.2\r\nExposure Count: N/A\r\nUnit IP Address: N/A\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\nDoctor explained this USB has been giving them intermittent connection issues since last week and more within the software rather than the actual hardware. He said they cant capture back to back within a series when this happens.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n03.07.2025          23:03:02            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\nSolution Description:\r\nConnected to OP2 and confirmed the PC recognizes USB is connected sensor config window also shows UBS but does not see sensor\r\nfound that they have to old twain drivers and the new IOSS all installed -- The IOSS driver was installed 6/24/2005 which is also around the same time issues started\r\ninquired about the new driver install: He stated that tracker helped them and installed the driver to work in their app\r\n\r\nremoved the old twain drivers (CDR twain, Schick 5.16 and AE USB\r\nfound core isolation enabled -- disabled and rebooted PC\r\n\r\nIt still hung up after first exposure (Tracker) and acquire button is grayed out\r\nReached out to teammate about the issue and was advised to check cable connectivity -- eliminated sensor as the issue since it works fine on another PC\r\nhe swapped out the USB box -- same thing: Acquire button in Tracker goes inactive after first exposure with sensor\r\n\r\nI connected to another PC with the same issue to at least check it like I did on OP2\r\nOP6:\r\n- disconnected sensor and USB\r\n- removed the old twain drivers\r\n- updated and installed missing prerequisites\r\n- disabled core isolation and rebooted PC\r\n\r\nconnected sensor after PC came back up\r\n- confirmed PC recognizes the USB\r\n- Sensor config sees both the USB and sensor\r\n\r\nhad him test in tracker -- works fine on this PC but he stated it works intermittently. OP2 was worse and does not allow to acquire back to back at all\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): Yes - Sensors and drivers are fine\r\nNOTE: Their issue is in Tracker\r\nhad him reach out to Tracker while Im on the line to see if they can assist -- he had to leave a VM for them\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n03.07.2025          22:12:32            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\nNote\r\n03.07.2025          22:12:32            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
      "excel_matched": true,
      "desc_primary_raw": "Software/Firmware/Driver",
      "desc_secondary_raw": "Software",
      "primary": "Software/Firmware/Driver",
      "secondary": "Software",
      "clarity": "clear",
      "tickets": 1,
      "classification_source": "ollama",
      "llm_classified": true,
      "spare_part_group": "",
      "major_issue_domain": "software",
      "major_issue_theme": "IOSS Performance / Slowness",
      "solution_path": "Software or plugin reinstalled/updated",
      "problem_description": "Warranty: unknown Dealer on-site: No Billable: No  - Canadian Customer Billing Accepted: N/A Billing Approved By: N/A Remote Access: Yes Sidexis Version: N/A Server Location: N/A PDATA Remote Location: N/A RCU Location (If Applicable): N/A Practice Management: Tracker Workstation(s): OP2 Scout Check: Yes Firmware: USB v. 1.5.140 / Sensor v. 3.4 Plug-in Version: IOSS 3.2 Exposure Count: N/A Unit IP Address: N/A Troubleshooting Description: Doctor explained this USB has been giving them intermittent connection issues since last week and more within the software rather than the actual hardware. He said they cant capture back to back within a series when this happens.",
      "problem_summary": "Doctor explained this USB has been giving them intermittent connection issues since last week and more within the software rather than the actual hardware. He said they cant capture back to back within a series when this happens. __________________",
      "solution_summary": "Connected to OP2 and confirmed the PC recognizes USB is connected sensor config window also shows UBS but does not see sensor found that they have to old twain drivers and the new IOSS all installed -- The IOSS driver was installed 6/24/2005 which is also around the same time issues started inquired about the new driver install: He stated that tracker helped them and installed the driver to work in their app removed the old twain drivers (CDR twain, Schick 5.16 and AE USB found core isolation enabled -- disabled and rebooted PC It still hung up after first exposure (Tracker) and acquire button is grayed out Reached out to teammate about the issue and was advised to check cable connectivity -- eliminated sensor as the issue since it works fine on another PC he swapped out the USB box -- same thing: Acquire button in Tracker goes inactive after first exposure with sensor I connected to another PC with the same issue to at least check it like I did on OP2 OP6: - disconnected sensor and USB - removed the old twain drivers - updated and installed missing prerequisites - disabled core isolation and rebooted PC connected sensor after PC came back up - confirmed PC recognizes the USB - Sensor config sees both the USB and sensor had him test in tracker -- works fine on this PC but he stated it works intermittently. OP2 was worse and does not allow to acquire back to back at all Functional (Yes/No): Yes - Sensors and drivers are fine NOTE: Their issue is in Tracker had him reach out to Tracker while Im on the line to see if they can assist -- he had to leave a VM for them __________________ Log 03.07.2025 22:12:32 Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO) Note 03.07.2025 22:12:32 Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO) __ Initial ticket creation __ __________________"
