      "notes_text": "Note\r\n07.07.2025          14:31:40            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n07.07.2025          14:31:39            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\nProblem Description\r\n03.07.2025          22:41:56            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\nContinuation of ticket 1253919\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n03.07.2025          22:41:56            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/03/2025 12:31:31 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Dr. Grace E. Rudersdorf,\r\nCallers Phone Number: 4029682567.\r\nCallers Role: Doctor\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Sensors disconnecting\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: I remoted into OP1 and 5.16 driver was found along with 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I removed all wiped folders and reinstalled only IOSS 3.2. Found corrupted C++ removed all reinstalled clean. Also found a work around for 2.0 remotes to work in Eaglesoft 24.\r\nSidexis 2.63 was found still to be installed. I uninstalled and wiped. Test shot successful but then stop working.\r\n\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP1 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files. A test shot was initially successful however, it stopped functioning afterward. Further evaluation may be needed if the issue persists.\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP2 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files.\r\n\r\n\r\nI remoted into OP3 and found the 5.16 driver installed along with the 2808 patch and IOSS 3.2. I proceeded to remove all related components, wiping associated folders, and then performed a clean reinstallation of only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nDuring the process, I identified corrupted Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables. I removed all versions and reinstalled the appropriate clean packages to ensure system integrity.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I discovered a workaround to allow 2.0 remotes to function correctly in Eaglesoft version 24.\r\n\r\nIts worth noting that Sidexis 2.63 was still installed on the system. I uninstalled it and performed a complete folder wipe to eliminate any residual files. A test shot was attempted but sensor stop being detected.\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up: I recommend replacing the USB interface.\r\n__________________",
