      "notes_text": "Note\r\n04.08.2025          21:25:40            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nClosing pending cable replacement\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n08.07.2025          18:55:29            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n08.07.2025          15:42:20            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nThis cable would need to be replaced with either a universal Schick 2.0 cable, PN B1209120, which may or may not be available as it is no longer in production, and relies entirely on existing stock.\r\n\r\nalternatively, if no parts are available, the entire sensor kit would need to be replaced, since the Schick Elite is not compatible with the Schick Conversion Kit that uses the 3.0 interface/cable.\r\n\r\nAdding PN B1209120 for replacement Schick 2.0 cable kit (6ft)\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now, this ticket can be reopened later if further troubleshooting/information is needed.\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n07.07.2025          16:05:52             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nSEE ATTACHED PICTURE OF BROKEN CABLE\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n07.07.2025          16:05:51             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nSEE ATTACHED PICTURE OF BROKEN CABLE\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n07.07.2025          16:05:51             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
