      "notes_text": "Note\r\n14.07.2025          14:23:29            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system may need to be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n08.07.2025          23:33:18            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n08.07.2025          23:33:16            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nFor this issue, wed want to verify that the USB hub has been tested on multiple ops, using USB 3.0 ports, ideally the original cables, and that the PCs are not small form factor if they are SFF, youd need to use a powered USB hub to ensure the unit is getting the power supply it needs.\r\n\r\nif this troubleshooting has been done, the unit may need to be replaced using PN 100008290. it is in warranty so once troubleshooting is verified, we can attach it to this ticket as a recommended spare part to be ordered.\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now, but we can reopen later for further troubleshooting.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n08.07.2025          19:22:04             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nno lights on usb hub\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n08.07.2025          19:22:03             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nno lights on usb hub\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n08.07.2025          19:22:03             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
