      "notes_text": "Note\r\n09.07.2025          19:00:33            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nClosing ticket as requested\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n09.07.2025          16:59:37            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n08.07.2025          21:26:28            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/08/2025 2:57:09 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: Yes\r\nDealer on-site:  No\r\nBillable: No\r\nBilling Accepted:   N/A\r\nBilling Approved By:  N/A\r\n\r\nRemote Access: Yes\r\nSidexis Version: N/A\r\nServer Location: N/A\r\nPDATA Remote Location: N/A\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable): N/A\r\nPractice Management: Dexis\r\nWorkstation(s): DESKTOP-KNIT5BAD\r\nScout Check: Yes\r\n\r\nFirmware: USB v. 1.5.121 to 1.5.141\r\nPlug-in Version: Schick 5.16 and AE 1.1\r\nExposure Count: N/A\r\nUnit IP Address: N/A\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\nthey have a sensor that intermittently loses connection when taking exposures back to back in series\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n08.07.2025          21:26:28            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\nSolution Description:\r\nConnected to workstation and checked s/w and plug-in compatibility\r\nshe stated these same sensors work in other rooms but it seems to only be this room, this sensor is assigned to the room\r\nthe sensor is currently recognized in AE utility tool\r\n\r\nfound that the SUI on USB needs to be updated removed the sensor and updated firmware\r\nreconnected but having issues with Twain recognizing the sensor\r\ntested with Twain Test and it shows no sensor detected as well device manager and AE utility still show sensor recognized\r\n\r\nhad her check if repair kit screwdriver is available and may have her clean contacts while I updated prerequisites\r\n.NET and MSXML were missing\r\nno cable kit to clean contacts -- rebooted PC\r\n\r\nallowed her to take multiple exposures, since she stated the issue is only with series exposures -- she took multiple in series without issues\r\nshe tested with another sensor to to confirm they also work\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): Yes\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n08.07.2025          20:57:36            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\nNote\r\n08.07.2025          20:57:36            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
