      "description_text": "xios xg sensor not working for multiples",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n11.07.2025          14:25:58            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n10.07.2025          16:48:18            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\n\r\nHello Service,\r\n\r\nplease see my notes from today:\r\n\r\n\r\nHello Filipe,\r\n\r\nI have tested your sensor working on reception pc today with multiple xrays, so this means the sensor and the software are working correctly.\r\n\r\nRegarding missing xrays , please see notes from earlier thisyear from my colleague Jack:\r\n\r\nConnected via TV to clinician PC and SERVER01.\r\nIT have replaced and upgraded Server to Windows 11 Pro without consulting compatibility.\r\nOld PDATA located in C:\\Images\\PDATA.\r\nAdvised Sidexis 4.3.1 isnt compatible with Windows 11 on Server and 4.4 upgrade will be required.\r\nLeft 4.3.1 installed on both PC so they can open create new records but advised they will not have access to old records until upgrade is purchased from Sident.\r\nThen the DB can be restored.\r\n\r\nIn order to merge the two databases you will need to contact Dentacs here:https://shop.dentacs.com/\r\nPlease also speak with Sident to advise you on upgrading to Sidexis 4.4,\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nDavid Balfour\r\nDigital Support Specialist\r\nField Sales\r\n01453 793190\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDavid.Balfour@dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\nwww.dentsplysirona.com\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n10.07.2025          16:47:04            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\nCustomer Note\r\n10.07.2025          16:47:04            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\n\r\nHello Filipe,\r\n\r\nI have tested your sensor working on reception pc today with multiple xrays, so this means the sensor and the software are working correctly.\r\n\r\nRegarding missing xrays , please see notes from earlier thisyear from my colleague Jack:\r\n\r\nConnected via TV to clinician PC and SERVER01.\r\nIT have replaced and upgraded Server to Windows 11 Pro without consulting compatibility.\r\nOld PDATA located in C:\\Images\\PDATA.\r\nAdvised Sidexis 4.3.1 isnt compatible with Windows 11 on Server and 4.4 upgrade will be required.\r\nLeft 4.3.1 installed on both PC so they can open create new records but advised they will not have access to old records until upgrade is purchased from Sident.\r\nThen the DB can be restored.\r\n\r\nIn order to merge the two databases you will need to contact Dentacs here:https://shop.dentacs.com/\r\nPlease also speak with Sident to advise you on upgrading to Sidexis 4.4,\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nDavid Balfour\r\nDigital Support Specialist\r\nField Sales\r\n01453 793190\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDavid.Balfour@dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\nwww.dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n10.07.2025          16:39:54            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\n\r\nTested Sensor working on Reception with multiple xrays,\r\nAdvised to contact Sident as no Teamviewer access and they use a differemt app for the Surgery pc.\r\nAdvised to update to Sidexis 4.4.\r\n__________________\r\nProblem Description\r\n10.07.2025          16:28:31            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\n\r\nXIOS XG sensor not working for multiples\r\nUnable to connect to surgery pc to test, so testing on Server pc (Server01)\r\nServer is running Windows11 and Sidexis 4.3.1\r\nDisabled Memory Integrity (core isolation) and tested sensor.\r\nTook test image from Server01 (reception)\r\n__________________",
