    {
      "ticket_id": "8001259100",
      "created_at": "2025-07-10",
      "record_type_group": "COMPLAINT",
      "region": "US",
      "language": "en",
      "category_level_2": "Schick 33 with AE USB",
      "category_level_3": "SW-Installation",
      "category_level_4": "Update / Installation issue",
      "firmware": "",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "documentation: unable to take images",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n14.07.2025          14:30:12            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n11.07.2025          23:50:38            Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN)\r\n\r\nOffice had a new CBCT installed 2 weeks ago and with it Sidexis 4.4 was installed as well.\r\n\r\nOffice is having issues on one PC with\r\nsensor now working while working on the rest. They were informed that Sirona no longer support the sensor due to it being a disconti\r\nnued SW. She provided me SN and confirmed it was a Schick 33 Sensor which is still support and will work with the new IOSS SW for Si\r\ndexis 4.\r\n\r\n I went ahead an reinstalled the IOSS SW on the system. We can run the Sirona Sensor configuration app and it shows the S\r\nensor connected. USB Module and Sensor up to date, both pass test and is ready for exposure. However when we go into Sidexis and try\r\n to take exposure it stays on Starting after selecting Interoral Sensor.\r\n\r\nAll indication show its connected and working but Sidex\r\nis 4.4 will not go further then starting even after waiting a few minutes.\r\n\r\nReached out to sirona and ended up getting Austin from\r\nSirona remoted into the system to troubleshoot and found the ViewsetConfiguration.xml was corrupted.\r\n\r\nTo resolve issue he removed th\r\ne XML and restarted service to resolve issue. We had office test scan and everything is working. They thanked me and are good to go\r\n\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n10.07.2025          19:43:00             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nOffice had a new CBCT installed 2 weeks ago and with it Sidexis 4.4 was installed as well.\r\n\r\nOffice is having issues on one PC with\r\nsensor now working while working on the rest. They were informed that Sirona no longer support the sensor due to it being a disconti\r\nnued SW. She provided me SN and confirmed it was a Schick 33 Sensor which is still support and will work with the new IOSS SW for Si\r\ndexis 4.\r\n\r\n I went ahead an reinstalled the IOSS SW on the system. We can run the Sirona Sensor configuration app and it shows the S\r\nensor connected. USB Module and Sensor up to date, both pass test and is ready for exposure. However when we go into Sidexis and try\r\n to take exposure it stays on Starting after selecting Interoral Sensor.\r\n\r\nAll indication show its connected and working but Sidex\r\nis 4.4 will not go further then starting even after waiting a few minutes.\r\n\r\nReached out to sirona and ended up getting Austin from\r\nSirona remoted into the system to troubleshoot and found the ViewsetConfiguration.xml was corrupted.\r\n\r\nTo resolve issue he removed th\r\ne XML and restarted service to resolve issue. We had office test scan and everything is working. They thanked me and are good to go\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n10.07.2025          19:42:59             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nOffice had a new CBCT installed 2 weeks ago and with it Sidexis 4.4 was installed as well.\r\n\r\nOffice is having issues on one PC with\r\nsensor now working while working on the rest. They were informed that Sirona no longer support the sensor due to it being a disconti\r\nnued SW. She provided me SN and confirmed it was a Schick 33 Sensor which is still support and will work with the new IOSS SW for Si\r\ndexis 4.\r\n\r\n I went ahead an reinstalled the IOSS SW on the system. We can run the Sirona Sensor configuration app and it shows the S\r\nensor connected. USB Module and Sensor up to date, both pass test and is ready for exposure. However when we go into Sidexis and try\r\n to take exposure it stays on Starting after selecting Interoral Sensor.\r\n\r\nAll indication show its connected and working but Sidex\r\nis 4.4 will not go further then starting even after waiting a few minutes.\r\n\r\nReached out to sirona and ended up getting Austin from\r\nSirona remoted into the system to troubleshoot and found the ViewsetConfiguration.xml was corrupted.\r\n\r\nTo resolve issue he removed th\r\ne XML and restarted service to resolve issue. We had office test scan and everything is working. They thanked me and are good to go\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n10.07.2025          19:42:59             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
      "excel_matched": true,
      "desc_primary_raw": "Info/Inquiry/How-to",
      "desc_secondary_raw": "General Inquiry",
      "primary": "Info/Inquiry/How-to",
      "secondary": "General Inquiry",
      "clarity": "clear",
      "tickets": 1,
      "classification_source": "keyword_fallback",
      "llm_classified": false,
      "spare_part_group": "",
      "major_issue_domain": "",
      "major_issue_theme": "",
      "solution_path": "Software or plugin reinstalled/updated",
      "problem_description": "Office had a new CBCT installed 2 weeks ago and with it Sidexis 4.4 was installed as well. Office is having issues on one PC with sensor now working while working on the rest. They were informed that Sirona no longer support the sensor due to it being a disconti nued SW. She provided me SN and confirmed it was a Schick 33 Sensor which is still support and will work with the new IOSS SW for Si dexis 4. I went ahead an reinstalled the IOSS SW on the system. We can run the Sirona Sensor configuration app and it shows the S ensor connected. USB Module and Sensor up to date, both pass test and is ready for exposure. However when we go into Sidexis and try to take exposure it stays on Starting after selecting Interoral Sensor. All indication show its connected and working but Sidex is 4.4 will not go further then starting even after waiting a few minutes. Reached out to sirona and ended up getting Austin from Sirona remoted into the system to troubleshoot and found the ViewsetConfiguration.xml was corrupted. To resolve issue he removed th e XML and restarted service to resolve issue. We had office test scan and everything is working. They thanked me and are good to go +++ +++ Log",
      "problem_summary": "documentation: unable to take images",
      "solution_summary": "n.a."
