      "major_issue_domain": "hardware",
      "major_issue_theme": "USB/Port/Communication Issue",
      "solution_path": "Other resolved action",
      "problem_description": "Warranty: Yes Dealer on-site: Yes Billable: No (Canada) Billing Accepted:  NA Billing Approved By:  NA 90 Day Expiration Date: 10/08/2025 Remote Access: Yes Practice Management: Safecom Troubleshooting Description: Remoted into SELK-DELL, and WS15-C. Every PC in the office has been having long standing intermittent connectivity issues with their sensors. All of our previous suggestions to the practice have been unsuccessful. - - The office has done the following: Using powered USB hubs. Removed Sentinel One anti-virus. Used a full sized tower (PC) vs the micro style they have now. Disabled USB power management settings. - - A common fix for the office is to restart the PC, or for one of our remote technicians to restart the Sirona Intraoral Service. Another Henry Schein technician in the past - Ted Kaltani - installed the legacy drivers on one PC and it worked for the entirety of the time they were installed on there. When IOSS v3.2 was re-installed (after removing the legacy driver) it started having intermittent connectivity again. - - The issue was unable to be replicated while I was remoted in and Stephen was on site. - - Logs for two PCs have been uploaded to attachments. Every PC in the office is having an issue. Several practices having issues since upgrading to IOSS plug-in after the legacy drivers. Requesting these logs be looked at by R&D for further investigation. Log Note __ Initial ticket creation __",
      "problem_summary": "Remoted into SELK-DELL, and WS15-C. Every PC in the office has been having long standing intermittent connectivity issues with their sensors. All of our previous suggestions to the practice have been unsuccessful. - - The office has done the following: Using powered USB hubs. Removed Sentinel One anti-virus. Used a full sized tower (PC) vs the micro style they have now. Disabled USB power management settings. - - A common fix for the office is to restart the PC, or for one of our remote technicians to restart the Sirona Intraoral Service. Another Henry Schein technician in the past - Ted Kaltani - installed the legacy drivers on one PC and it worked for the entirety of the time they were installed on there. When IOSS v3.2 was re-installed (after removing the legacy driver) it started having intermittent connectivity again. - - The issue was unable to be replicated while I was remoted in and Stephen was on site. - - Logs for two PCs have been uploaded to attachments. Every PC in the office is having an issue. Several practices having issues since upgrading to IOSS plug-in after the legacy drivers. Requesting these logs be looked at by R&D for further investigation. __________________ Log 10.07.2025 22:44:30 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) Note 10.07.2025 22:44:30 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Initial ticket creation __ __________________",
      "solution_summary": "Requesting logs be evaluated by R&D further. Logs uploaded to attachments. *** Could not select unknown further investigation required it would not allow me to save ticket *** Functional (Yes/No): Yes (intermittently) __________________"
    },
