      "category_level_4": "Intermittent Operation / Connectivity",
      "firmware": "",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "spare part: ptc proc rma 3 ae remotes- n",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n07.08.2025          15:02:26            Michael Hall (MHALL)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nSolution Description: closed ticket per Jen Brown\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No):\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n07.08.2025          12:47:04            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n30.07.2025          22:28:53            Jerome Miller (JMILLER1)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/30/2025 4:15:45 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: San S\r\nCallers Phone Number:\r\nCallers Role: Staff\r\n\r\nWarranty Status:yes\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\n\r\nProblem Description:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description:Connected to Desktop-Io3p9f8 tested the sensors and it was working\r\nwent over basic troublehooting and what to look for with the customer.\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No):yes\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n12.07.2025          00:00:40            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n12.07.2025          00:00:38            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nFrom the sound of the issue, It is worth noting that on occasion these Schick 3.0 USB modules can not function properly if they dont have the full USB 3.0 power spec if these are small form factor PCs or laptops, a reasonable troubleshooting step could be to try using powered USB 3.0 hubs, to ensure the module receives the output it needs.\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now, but we can reopen later if further troubleshooting is needed.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n11.07.2025          16:51:20             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nDetails: in dilemma\r\n3 REMOTES-- NO POWER TO ANY OF THE 3\r\n\r\n\r\n2815130019\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nID: 1973071305\r\nPW: jvxyfm96\r\n\r\n\r\nID: 804093739\r\nPW: dyhabhqt\r\nU\r\nSB 3.0 remote: 2030799 kit: WS10001582\r\nUSB 3.0: 2036904 kit: EL20001411\r\nUSB3.0: 2034510 kit: WS20005034\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIssue Reported: Power\r\nsurge\r\n\r\nEquipment Type and Model: Schick USB 3.0 Remote.\r\n\r\nSerial Number: 2030799\r\n\r\nAcquisition Software & Version: Eaglesoft\r\n\r\nIssue i\r\nn One or All Rooms: ALL\r\n\r\nOther Sensors work with working Remotes in Room(s) with Issue: Y\r\n\r\nPC Name: DESKTOP-20s655g\r\n\r\nSchick Driver V\r\nersion (Programs and features): AE USB INTERFACE\r\n\r\nRemote FW/FPGA Version: NA Sensor FW Version:  NA\r\n\r\nIf Remote Issue: YES\r\n\r\n2.0 or 3.\r\n0: Tried Different USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: YES\r\n\r\nOffice claims they worked with sirona and sirona said all t\r\nheir remotes were dead.......\r\nstarted call working on DESKTOP-20S655G saw the USB power error pop up,\r\nrestarted PC and checked driv\r\ner installations and then had them try different remote.\r\nSame issue.\r\nMigrated to computer: CHECKIN-PC. able to get one remote to let\r\n me do a firmware update(2036904). Plugged in second remote. Same issues happening. Usb power error appears in windows.\r\nwhen I resta\r\nrted the PC after this asked them to plug in (2036904) this remote now gives the same USB power issue.\r\ntried with different cable th\r\nat connects USB remote to PC same issue.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n11.07.2025          16:51:19             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nDetails: in dilemma\r\n3 REMOTES-- NO POWER TO ANY OF THE 3\r\n\r\n\r\n2815130019\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nID: 1973071305\r\nPW: jvxyfm96\r\n\r\n\r\nID: 804093739\r\nPW: dyhabhqt\r\nU\r\nSB 3.0 remote: 2030799 kit: WS10001582\r\nUSB 3.0: 2036904 kit: EL20001411\r\nUSB3.0: 2034510 kit: WS20005034\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nIssue Reported: Power\r\nsurge\r\n\r\nEquipment Type and Model: Schick USB 3.0 Remote.\r\n\r\nSerial Number: 2030799\r\n\r\nAcquisition Software & Version: Eaglesoft\r\n\r\nIssue i\r\nn One or All Rooms: ALL\r\n\r\nOther Sensors work with working Remotes in Room(s) with Issue: Y\r\n\r\nPC Name: DESKTOP-20s655g\r\n\r\nSchick Driver V\r\nersion (Programs and features): AE USB INTERFACE\r\n\r\nRemote FW/FPGA Version: NA Sensor FW Version:  NA\r\n\r\nIf Remote Issue: YES\r\n\r\n2.0 or 3.\r\n0: Tried Different USB Cable/USB Port/Bypassed USB hubs/Extenders: YES\r\n\r\nOffice claims they worked with sirona and sirona said all t\r\nheir remotes were dead.......\r\nstarted call working on DESKTOP-20S655G saw the USB power error pop up,\r\nrestarted PC and checked driv\r\ner installations and then had them try different remote.\r\nSame issue.\r\nMigrated to computer: CHECKIN-PC. able to get one remote to let\r\n me do a firmware update(2036904). Plugged in second remote. Same issues happening. Usb power error appears in windows.\r\nwhen I resta\r\nrted the PC after this asked them to plug in (2036904) this remote now gives the same USB power issue.\r\ntried with different cable th\r\nat connects USB remote to PC same issue.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n11.07.2025          16:51:19             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
