      "notes_text": "Note\r\n18.07.2025          15:24:24            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nIt cannot be determined from the information provided if this issue is software or hardware related.  It will be kept as a service ticket unless additional information can be provided by the customer.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n14.07.2025          15:27:50            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n14.07.2025          15:27:48            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nHello!\r\n\r\nI would first want to verify if other USB modules work on the same PC, and if this issue follows the module in question when on other PCs small form factor computers and laptops can often have issues delivering adequate power so a powered USB 3.0 hub may be needed. If it turns out none of that is the issue, we can then approve for an RMA and replace the module.\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now, we can reopen later if further troubleshooting is needed.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n11.07.2025          20:09:14             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nWindows recognizes device is plugged in but does not stay connected. light flickers to green and then back to amber.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n11.07.2025          20:09:13             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nWindows recognizes device is plugged in but does not stay connected. light flickers to green and then back to amber.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n11.07.2025          20:09:13             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
