      "description_text": "sensor sometimes not working",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n15.07.2025          19:52:01            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          17:17:59            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/14/2025 11:09:18 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Sharon Hines\r\nCallers Phone Number: 847-882-3360\r\nCallers Role:Staff\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\nPart number request.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nWe discussed issue.\r\nThey will call back to check software versions on pc and firmware on 3.0 Interface.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\nGave part number for wire and repair kit.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n14.07.2025          17:17:51            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/14/2025 11:09:18 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Sharon Hines\r\nCallers Phone Number: 847-882-3360\r\nCallers Role:Staff\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\nPart number request.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nWe discussed issue.\r\nThey will call back to check software versions on pc and firmware on 3.0 Interface.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\nGave part number for wire and repair kit.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\nProblem Description\r\n14.07.2025          17:12:16            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\nCustomer states their Schick 33 S0 sensor is not working correctly. It will sometimes not be detected by the USB module. Other times\r\n it will take an image, and they can see the image, but then it disappears and does not save in Dexis. I asked the customer if these\r\n issues happen at different workstations with different USB modules, and they said it does. They also said that their other Schick sensor all have had no issues.\r\n\r\nI had the customer try to repeat the issue, but it is currently working. I then had them change out\r\nthe sensor cable, and the sensor is still working currently. I instructed them to continue to use the sensor, and call back if the issue persists. If the issues are resolved, then the sensor cable is the issue, and they will call back to get the cable replaced.\r\n\r\n+\r\n++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n14.07.2025          16:09:54             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nCustomer states their Schick 33 S0 sensor is not working correctly. It will sometimes not be detected by the USB module. Other times\r\n it will take an image, and they can see the image, but then it disappears and does not save in Dexis. I asked the customer if these\r\n issues happen at different workstations with different USB modules, and they said it does. They also said that their other Schick s\r\nensor all have had no issues.\r\n\r\nI had the customer try to repeat the issue, but it is currently working. I then had them change out\r\nthe sensor cable, and the sensor is still working currently. I instructed them to continue to use the sensor, and call back if the i\r\nssue persists. If the issues are resolved, then the sensor cable is the issue, and they will call back to get the cable replaced.\r\n\r\n+\r\n++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n14.07.2025          16:09:53             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
