      "category_level_3": "SW-Installation",
      "category_level_4": "Update / Installation support",
      "firmware": "",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "new op not working with schick sensors",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n15.07.2025          19:53:12            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n14.07.2025          16:48:18            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/14/2025 10:35:24 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: YES\r\nDealer on-site: NO\r\nBillable: NO\r\nBilling Accepted: No\r\nDetails: 3rd party connection support with XVcapture and Denticon\r\n\r\nFollow Up:\r\n\r\nPractice needed assistance setting up a new PC, PlanetDDS support tried to assist, but I think they missed a couple of details, they tried telling the practice their hardware may be outdated/broken.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n14.07.2025          16:48:18            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n\r\nUninstalled AE USB driver, theyre using 2.0 hubs so only Schick 33/Elite driver 5.16 is needed, plus CDR Twain and CDR Patch 2808, which were already installed.\r\n\r\nprereqs were missing so I updated those, reinstalled MSXML to 4.0 SP3, and removed/reapplied the CDR Patch. Core isolation was also still on, I disabled that as well and rebooted.\r\n\r\nafter the reboot, the sensor was picking up just fine in TWAIN test, worked as expected in XVCapture.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n14.07.2025          16:36:10            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          16:36:10            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
