      "notes_text": "Note\r\n14.08.2025          22:24:30            Seth Woodward (SWOODWARD)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  08/14/2025 1:17:52 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Daniel Ektevez\r\nCallers Phone Number: 917-903-0126\r\nCallers Role:  IT\r\n\r\nWarranty Status: Yes\r\nBilling Previously Accepted: NA\r\n\r\nProblem Description: assisting with upgrade to 4.4 and IOSS 3.2\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description: logged on to SERVER2012\r\nconfirmed this server operating system is Server2016 not 2012\r\nconfirmed they have a backup of PDATA\r\n4.4 reg number provided by James\r\nstarted the upgrade - passwords save to desktop and PDATA\r\nfailed the upgrade to sql 2017\r\nskipped the SQL upgrade for now\r\nhad some trouble during the upgrade - couldnt rename PDATA - S4ADMIN password errors but eventually the upgrade was successful\r\n\r\nlogged on to IRAHAL-PANROOM\r\nupgraded to 4.4\r\nuninstalled sidexis 4 sensor plugin 2.2\r\ninstalled IOSS 3.2 - installed properly but not connecting to the sidexis service in the configuration app\r\nfound the domain firewall was on on SERVER2012 - after i turned it off we could connect\r\n\r\nlogged on to ROOM-2-2024\r\nupgraded to 4.4 and IOSS 3.2 also had to upgrade the video module plugin for their mouthwatch cameras\r\ntook test exposures - successful\r\n\r\nhe will take care of the rest of the workstations\r\n\r\nSolution Description: upgrade to 4.4 and IOSS 3.2\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): Yes\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n13.08.2025          20:45:08            Seth Woodward (SWOODWARD)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  08/13/2025 2:42:40 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Daniel Ektevez\r\nCallers Phone Number: 917-903-0126\r\nCallers Role: IT\r\n\r\nWarranty Status:\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\n\r\nProblem Description: wanted to schedule the sidexis 4.4 upgrade\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description: going to call back tomorrow at 12:30 for the upgrade\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No):\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n01.08.2025          17:52:00            Michael Hall (MHALL)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  08/01/2025 11:31:07 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Ray Santos\r\nCallers Phone Number: 9179030126\r\nCallers Role:\r\n\r\nWarranty Status: yes\r\nBilling Previously Accepted: na\r\n\r\nProblem Description: IT unblocked port in question and still having the issue\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description: got James Malloy logged in and did not find anything definitive with wireshark but did find a TLS issue ran patch and tested without rebooting the server(office seeing patients)  and still failed recommended rebooting the server and testing to see if that helps if not we can upgrade to 4.4 and IOSS 3.2 after that,\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description: reboot server and test if issue persists upgrade to 4.4 and IOSS 3.2 James Malloy can provide a reg # for upgrade,\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): yes\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n22.07.2025          17:16:26            Robert Jean (RJEAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nRay wanted to know what was done, advised we told IT to open the firewall port to allow flow.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.07.2025          15:31:25            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n15.07.2025          18:01:29            Seth Woodward (SWOODWARD)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/15/2025 11:42:48 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Daniel E (IT)\r\nCallers Phone Number: 914-375-3009\r\nCallers Role: IT\r\n\r\nWarranty Status:\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\n\r\nProblem Description: Daniel was looking for info on what needs to be corrected on the server\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description: i forwarded him info on the URL that cant be accessed by the workstation  and the port number\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No):\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          23:10:32            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\nIn talking with James, IT may have too much security blocking free flow of data.\r\nDo tasks in ticket and reach out to him if that does not fix the issue.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n14.07.2025          22:53:13            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\nIT will call back to get us on server to run DB cleanup and check for Sidexis user.\r\n__________________\r\nProblem Description\r\n14.07.2025          22:52:11            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\nIntermittent connection\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/14/2025 2:02:21 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: Yes\r\nDealer on-site: Yes\r\nBillable: No\r\n\r\nRemote Access: yes\r\nSidexis Version: 4.3.1\r\nServer Location:SERVER2012\r\nPDATA Remote Location:SERVER2012\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable):\r\nPractice Management: Dentrix\r\nWorkstation(s): Room-2-2024\r\nScout Check: Attached\r\n\r\nFirmware: 1.5.140\r\nPlug-in Version: 2.2.\r\nRenamed Schick folder in Program Data and reinstalled 2.2 plug-in.\r\nTested in Sidexis.\r\n\r\nSensor #15025988\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nShut off power management on USB ports.\r\nUsed Tech toolbox to install missing C++.\r\nRebooted.\r\n\r\nTested.\r\nHe takes an image and then Sidexis stays red.\r\nCan get one or two.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\nCalled tech on his phone.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          22:46:34            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/14/2025 2:24:19 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Ray Santos\r\nCallers Phone Number: 347\r\nCallers Role: Dealer tech\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\nCalled back tech on his cell.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nSince basic TS did not solve issue, I removed SW and drivers and uninstalled CDR DICOM and renamed folders.\r\nReinstalled 2.2 and see sensor correctly.\r\nRebooted.\r\n\r\nTested.\r\nStill fails.\r\n\r\nRan Client provisioning.\r\nPasses.\r\nEvents in PC\r\nRan SFC and it repaired files.\r\n\r\nRebooted and tested.\r\nStill stops after one or 2 images.\r\nTested with different USB Interface. Same.\r\n\r\nHad him switch sensors and it is working.\r\nHad him check screws on sensor #15025988: tight.\r\nHe changed elastomer and it did three and stopped.\r\n\r\nI had him inspect and change wire.\r\nStill failing. He went to another room and it is doing the same thing.\r\n25064519 & 15025988 does not work.\r\n\r\nSize zero works all size 2 fail.\r\nChatted with James and he suggested I look at server and run Sidexis 4 DB Backup Sidexis 4 Cleanup and Sidexis 4 Maintenance. Check if Sidexis4serviceuser is present in Domain users.\r\nWhen I try to go to https://server2012:42929/sirona/gbe/817bb19c-95cb-40f3-9501-b7baa1d35cc5/v4/ it asks for login. Sidexis4 service fails.\r\n\r\nIT will call in to get us on server.\r\nSee attached sensor log.\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n14.07.2025          20:04:22            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          20:04:22            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
