      "notes_text": "Note\r\n21.07.2025          17:47:25            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nIT Called back and stated the issue is still occurring with the replacement parts\r\nVerified multiple computers have thew issue with the sabe interface\r\nFound that they only have 1 USB Cable - suspected it is the USB cable\r\nProvided the PN for a USB cable - B2250151\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n17.07.2025          15:00:25            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n14.07.2025          22:36:03            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/14/2025 4:30:59 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: YES\r\nDealer on-site: NO\r\nBillable: NO\r\nBilling Accepted: NA\r\nBilling Approved By: NA\r\n90 Day Expiration Date: 10/12/2025\r\n\r\nRemote Access: YES\r\nSidexis Version: 4.3.1\r\nServer Location: SONIVA-AF-SVR\r\nPDATA Remote Location: SONIVA-AF-SVR\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable): NA\r\nPractice Management: NA\r\nWorkstation(s): ROOM1\r\nScout Check: NA, SCHICK SENSORS\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\n\r\nPractice has 2 sensor kits with differing issues:\r\n\r\nS2 sensor - 3.0\r\nsn: 2050955\r\nno signs of life, computers panic with a power draw error stating its pulling more power than the USB port can provide. theyve tried multiple USB ports, PCs, and USB cables, same results. port feels loose and its likely a broken USB connection with pads bridging to ground, causing the USB port to dump current straight to ground and overload its limits.\r\n\r\nS1 sensor 2.0 - intermittent connection\r\ntheyre able to see the sensor, but the second they move the sensor cable around, it immediately disconnects.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n14.07.2025          22:36:03            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n\r\nFor the 3.0 sensor, approving for RMA: 100008290 (also throwing in some cable clips)\r\n\r\nfor the 2.0, this sensor kit is older, so its out of warranty, and they just need to purchase a new sensor conversion kit for it.  PN 100008720\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n14.07.2025          22:10:12            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\nNote\r\n14.07.2025          22:10:12            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
