      "notes_text": "Note\r\n13.08.2025          15:11:40            Michael Hall (MHALL)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nSolution Description: issue resolved\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No):\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n13.08.2025          13:10:25            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n17.07.2025          17:43:04            Melvin Felix (MFELIX)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/17/2025 11:07:23 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Alex Downton\r\nCallers Phone Number: 7097251876\r\nCallers Role: Patterson Tech\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request: Sensor drops off when opening up CDRdicom.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details: I remoted into DT-01L2DT I found Schick elite 5.13 driver installed with IOSS 3.2. I uninstalled 5.13 driver and IOSS 3.2 wiped the folder and reinstalled only IOSS 3.2.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up: Test shots in Sidexis successful. tested with CDR open no issues acquiring in Sidexis.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n16.07.2025          23:56:43            Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN)\r\n\r\nOffice need to call and we need to remote to check the software and workstation C++, MSXML SP\r\n\r\nPlease give support a call\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n16.07.2025          15:02:55             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nUsers still having issues with Sidexis not being able to capture images sometimes. Issue happens on multiple workstations with diffe\r\nrent sensors. In this case the user was able to take the first 3 bitewings but then it never went green to capture the 4th. I have d\r\neleted the acquisition modules from CDR and deleted the old drivers but the issue still happens intermittently.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n16.07.2025          15:02:54             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nUsers still having issues with Sidexis not being able to capture images sometimes. Issue happens on multiple workstations with diffe\r\nrent sensors. In this case the user was able to take the first 3 bitewings but then it never went green to capture the 4th. I have d\r\neleted the acquisition modules from CDR and deleted the old drivers but the issue still happens intermittently.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n16.07.2025          15:02:54             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
