      "notes_text": "Solution Description\r\n25.08.2025          09:03:21            Pablo Taibi (DIVGU798)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n25.08.2025          09:03:17            Pablo Taibi (DIVGU798)\r\n\r\nHello Alberto,\r\n\r\nIt looks like the USB voltage is breaking down here.\r\n\r\nPlease try a USB connection at the back of the PC.\r\nIf this does not help,\r\n\r\ninstall an ACTIVE USB amplifier.\r\n\r\nI think the sensor is not getting enough current.\r\n\r\nBest regards\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n11.08.2025          14:46:37            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket upon resolution with the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n11.08.2025          08:00:18            Thomas Waldraff (DIGSJ847)\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nIt looks like the USB voltage is breaking down here.\r\n\r\nPlease try a USB connection at the back of the PC.\r\nIf this does not help,\r\n\r\ninstall an ACTIVE USB amplifier.\r\n\r\nI think the sensor is not getting enough current.\r\n\r\nbr Thomas\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n17.07.2025          14:02:40             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nGood morning\r\n\r\nwe wait for your answer\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n17.07.2025          12:28:12            Maria Daniela Ferreira Catoira (DIPTU543)\r\n\r\nhello Team\r\n\r\nCustomer complains error with Xios sensor\r\na few days ago the cable was changed and it worked correctly for a few da\r\nys.\r\nNow the error is the same as before changing the cable\r\nI attach video so you can confirm the status.\r\n\r\nWhat would be the recommendation?\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustome