    {
      "ticket_id": "8001262447",
      "created_at": "2025-07-16",
      "record_type_group": "INQUIRY",
      "region": "US",
      "language": "en",
      "category_level_2": "Schick 33 with AE USB",
      "category_level_3": "General User/Technician information requested",
      "category_level_4": "Technician information requested",
      "firmware": "",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "hub will not connect to sensor",
      "notes_text": "Solution Description\r\n17.07.2025          15:31:02            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n17.07.2025          15:31:01            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nFor troubleshooting this I would probably suggest calling our main support line, but a couple of things to try could be:\r\n\r\nIf theyre using the legacy Schick drivers (33/Elite USB driver 5.16 or AE USB 1.1)\r\n - Checking for 12th gen or higher intel CPU and installing MSXML parser (if not already present) and the CDR Patch\r\n- Disabling Core Isolation in windows settings\r\n- verifying firmware is up to date using the Firmware Update tool, which I see may have already been checked. you do have to use the update tool though, as the legacy driver utilities do not know the newest firmware. youd be looking for version 1.5.140.\r\n\r\nif theyre running IOSS:\r\n- verify theyre running IOSS v3.2\r\n- can also try Core Isolation here as well\r\n- ensure no legacy drivers are installed that could be conflicting with IOSS\r\n\r\nIt could also be a hardware issue, so typical elimination testing could be performed of reseating the sensor cable on the sensor, swapping for a known functional one, swapping the USB module, making sure youre using USB 3.0 and/or a powered USB hub, etc.\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now we can reopen later if further troubleshooting is needed.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n16.07.2025          20:46:20             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nrunning latest firmware\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n16.07.2025          20:46:19             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nrunning latest firmware\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n16.07.2025          20:46:19             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
      "excel_matched": true,
      "desc_primary_raw": "Connectivity/Recognition",
      "desc_secondary_raw": "Sensor Detection Failure (Persistent)",
      "primary": "Connectivity/Recognition",
      "secondary": "Sensor Detection Failure (Persistent)",
      "clarity": "clear",
      "tickets": 1,
      "classification_source": "ollama",
      "llm_classified": true,
      "spare_part_group": "",
      "major_issue_domain": "hardware",
      "major_issue_theme": "USB/Port/Communication Issue",
      "solution_path": "Other resolved action",
      "problem_description": "running latest firmware +++ +++ Log",
      "problem_summary": "hub will not connect to sensor",
      "solution_summary": "via Customer Notes __________________ Customer Note 17.07.2025 15:31:01 Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904) For troubleshooting this I would probably suggest calling our main support line, but a couple of things to try could be: If theyre using the legacy Schick drivers (33/Elite USB driver 5.16 or AE USB 1.1) - Checking for 12th gen or higher intel CPU and installing MSXML parser (if not already present) and the CDR Patch - Disabling Core Isolation in windows settings - verifying firmware is up to date using the Firmware Update tool, which I see may have already been checked. you do have to use the update tool though, as the legacy driver utilities do not know the newest firmware. youd be looking for version 1.5.140. if theyre running IOSS: - verify theyre running IOSS v3.2 - can also try Core Isolation here as well - ensure no legacy drivers are installed that could be conflicting with IOSS It could also be a hardware issue, so typical elimination testing could be performed of reseating the sensor cable on the sensor, swapping for a known functional one, swapping the USB module, making sure youre using USB 3.0 and/or a powered USB hub, etc. Closing ticket for now we can reopen later if further troubleshooting is needed. __________________ Customer Note 16.07.2025 20:46:20 CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO) running latest firmware +++ +++ __________________"
    },
