    {
      "ticket_id": "8001263361",
      "created_at": "2025-07-17",
      "record_type_group": "COMPLAINT",
      "region": "US",
      "language": "en",
      "category_level_2": "Schick 33 with AE USB",
      "category_level_3": "Image quality",
      "category_level_4": "Partial image",
      "firmware": "1.5.140",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "old pt/new pt & image slow. schick senso",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n03.09.2025          21:00:59            Sebastian Cedeno (SCEDENO)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  09/03/2025 2:27:13 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Nicholas Claessens (Curve) Hanah office\r\nCallers Phone Number: 8889104376\r\nCallers Role: Curve Support\r\n\r\nWarranty Status: yes\r\nBilling Previously Accepted: no\r\n\r\nProblem Description: Nick from Curve called because images keep getting into rescue mode, cant acquire afterwards\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:  remoted into S4K-GJ-XRAY, checked logs, getting a few of these:\r\n\r\n2025-09-03 12:17:00,322 WebApiService.Helpers.ClientHeartbeatMonitor`1               [56] ERROR - Heartbeat Monitor exception\r\n\r\nChecked Device Manager, turned off all USB power saving.\r\nChecked uptime, 16 days.\r\nRestarted intraoral sensor service, they are now able to acquire.\r\n\r\nSolution Description: restarting the service fixed the issue.\r\nRecommended restarting the PC at least once a week\r\nAsked Hanah about the AE clip, she states she never got it.\r\nRecommended to contact the dealer to order one with ticket number from last time.\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): Yes. Nick got the contact info for the Integration Team support.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n25.08.2025          18:43:53            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nConference/Troubleshooting call\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting timing in-between images captured and image quality\r\n\r\nWhile using the legacy Schick Driver 1.1.333, the office had a 1 to 2 second wait in-between the end of the exposure and the display of the taken image.  With IOSS 3.2, they have a 8 to 20 second wait until the image is displayed on the screen.\r\n\r\nCurve support tech updated Curve Capture to the latest version and adjusted the Sharpness and Filter within Curve - those are the only two modifications from Curves support.  There was no change in the time to display the image on the screen.  They were not able to provide any log files from curve for our troubleshooting.\r\n\r\nAfter acquiring more information regarding the image quality issue, I was informed they use Gendex GX-770 tubehead that are well aged and may be experiencing issues while emitting radiation\r\n\r\nWith this being noted, we discovered the use of the legacy Schick driver allowed our filters to be applied to the image prior to the image being added to Curve.  This was modifying the image enough for the office to receive images that appeared to be better quality and compensate for the potential issues with the tube heads.\r\n\r\nThe issue of the failure of an acquisition of an image is likely due to the potential issues with the GX-770.  They will have a technetium come onsite and verify the GX-770s.\r\n\r\nNo changes were preformed on IOSS/Schick software/Hardware\r\n\r\nIT support requested an email from DS explaining any explanations on the issues.\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n20.08.2025          16:16:26            Sebastian Cedeno (SCEDENO)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  08/20/2025 10:03:19 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Ken Mitchell\r\nCallers Phone Number: 9706404266\r\nCallers Role: office IT\r\n\r\nWarranty Status: yes\r\nBilling Previously Accepted: no\r\n\r\nProblem Description: Ken called very upset about the integration, he is reporting these issues:\r\nStill getting image quality issues\r\nLarger ones very fuzzy\r\nThey press the button to fire, its taking pretty long.\r\nSometimes they need to acquire twice.\r\nHe also states they are still getting ghost images, but that seems to be with legacy drivers on other workstations.\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description: remoted into S4K-GJ-XRAY, checked Schick sensor settings, image filter was not applied.\r\nI suggested adding the General filter for Schick 33, but he was adamant we need to find a solution between us and Curve.\r\n\r\nSolution Description: I attached the original and optimized image from Curve to the ticket (both look similar)\r\nEmailed Ken (CCd Jeff) and asked for an official answer on what to do next.\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): Yes, not sure if image quality will improve with filter applied.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.08.2025          19:35:36            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nCalled Ken on scheduled call\r\nConnected to S4K-GJ-XRAY\r\nFound CDR Twain and AE 1..1.333 driver installed\r\nWe called Curve and confirmed IOSS 3.2 will work - CONFIRMED YES\r\nThere was a partial install of Sidexis still in place (ERLang and SQL)\r\nRemoved all of Sidexis leftovers\r\nFound duplicate/redundant C++ installations\r\nRemoved all of c++ and reinstalled\r\nFound firmware was on 1.5.121\r\nInstalled IOSS 3.2\r\nUpdated to 1.5.140\r\nSensor displays in Curve\r\nTest captures are ok\r\nOffice will back in operation om Wednesday\r\nThey will inform IT if there are further issues\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n14.08.2025          22:14:29            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nAustin Out of office\r\nI contacted Ken and scheduled a time to resolve the issue\r\n8/18\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n05.08.2025          14:59:38            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nclosing ticket per J. Brown\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n05.08.2025          14:22:24            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has previously been identified and is being investigated under CAPA 2024-532.  Further evaluation of individual complaints will be conducted as required.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n************************Safety Task ************************\r\n\r\n\t\r\n\tNote\r\n\t05.08.2025          14:21:16            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\t\r\n\tBased on the ticket information, there is no injury to the patient or user.  The image acquired contains a full previous image or a portion of previous and current image or a blank image which is identifiable.  It is not possible for a dentist to provide treatment based on the image acquired and the dentist would need to retake another image to provide treatment.  Therefore, there is no risk to the patient for unnecessary treatment and the risk of additional radiation exposure is assessed as part of the product risk management and there are no immediate or long-range consequences.\r\n\tThis complaint is evaluated to be Not Reportable within USA and ROW. The issue is being evaluated under CAPA-2024-532.\r\n\t\r\n\t__________________\r\n\r\n************************************************\r\n\r\n\r\n\tLog\r\n\t30.07.2025          00:17:03            Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA)\r\n************************************************\r\n\r\n\r\n\tNote\r\n\t30.07.2025          00:17:03            Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA)\r\n\t\r\n\tFrom: Stevens, Austin <Austin.Stevens@dentsplysirona.com>\r\n\tSent: Friday, July 25, 2025 6:45 PM\r\n\tTo: kmitchell@sequent-is.com\r\n\tCc: jakeallen@curvedental.com Mandia, Jeffrey <Jeffrey.Mandia@dentsplysirona.com> Almond, Timothy <Timothy.Almond@dentsplysirona.com>\r\n\tSubject: Re: Curve Integration\r\n\t\r\n\tHello Ken & Jake,\r\n\t\r\n\tThanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids.\r\n\tToday we talked about two issues the office is currently facing.\r\n\t\r\n\t1. Previous patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room\r\n\t2. Poor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in\r\n\t\r\n\tAs discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem.\r\n\tSince this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related.\r\n\tIf moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question.\r\n\t\r\n\tWeve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve.\r\n\tThe room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in.\r\n\t\r\n\tWhile discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance.\r\n\tAt this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve.\r\n\t\r\n\tThe ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361.\r\n\tThank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer.\r\n\t\r\n\tWarm Regards,\r\n\t\r\n\tAustin Stevens\r\n\tTechnical Support Specialist, Imaging\r\n\t\r\n\t__________________\r\n\t\r\n************************************************\r\n\r\nNote\r\n30.07.2025          00:36:18            Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n\r\nOld patient/New patient image issues and slowness taking images. Schick sensors, 3.0 integration to Curve\r\n\r\n\r\nFrom: Stevens, Austin <Austin.Stevens@dentsplysirona.com>\r\nSent: Friday, July 25, 2025 6:45 PM\r\nTo: kmitchell@sequent-is.com\r\nCc: jakeallen@curvedental.com Mandia, Jeffrey <Jeffrey.Mandia@dentsplysirona.com> Almond, Timothy <Timothy.Almond@dentsplysirona.com>\r\nSubject: Re: Curve Integration\r\n\r\nHello Ken & Jake,\r\n\r\nThanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids.\r\nToday we talked about two issues the office is currently facing.\r\n\r\n1. Previous patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room\r\n2. Poor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in\r\n\r\nAs discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem.\r\nSince this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related.\r\nIf moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question.\r\n\r\nWeve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve.\r\nThe room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in.\r\n\r\nWhile discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance.\r\nAt this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve.\r\n\r\nThe ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361.\r\nThank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer.\r\n\r\nWarm Regards,\r\n\r\nAustin Stevens\r\nTechnical Support Specialist, Imaging\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n29.07.2025          18:09:30            Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nTracking number sent to Ken for visibility.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n28.07.2025          23:07:21            Carol Cowles (CCOWLES)\r\n\r\nitem shipped\r\nOrder 3415131\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n28.07.2025          21:57:19            Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n*********** S/N of the affected USB Interface is 2048782. This is not showing up in DSCRM for me to be able to attach to the ticket. ***********\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n28.07.2025          21:55:22            Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nKen reached out and said PTC he had trouble ordering another interface as they werent aware of any issues.\r\nKen says he provided PTC the ticket number as well.\r\n- -\r\nSending this to order service for processing.\r\nPlease send the USB 3.0 interface directly to the practice.\r\n- -\r\nThanks!\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n28.07.2025          18:44:36            Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nRMA for affected USB interface recommended.\r\nThey will proceed with the RMA of the USB interface due to old patient / new patient issue.\r\nS/N of USB Interface could not be found in DSCRM at the time of the call.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n26.07.2025          13:07:12            Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/26/2025 7:06:32 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCalled and spoke with Ken from IT and Jake from Curve Dental.\r\nSee below for email recap:\r\n\r\nHello Ken & Jake,\r\n\r\nThanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids.\r\nToday we talked about two issues the office is currently facing.\r\n\r\nPrevious patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room\r\nPoor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in\r\n\r\nAs discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem.\r\nSince this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related.\r\nIf moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question.\r\n\r\nWeve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve.\r\nThe room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in.\r\n\r\nWhile discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance.\r\nAt this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve.\r\n\r\nThe ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361.\r\nThank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer.\r\n\r\nWarm Regards,\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n23.07.2025          18:25:19            Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/23/2025 11:58:55 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Ken Mitchell\r\nCallers Phone Number: 9706404266\r\nCallers Role: Office IT admin\r\n\r\nBilling Previously Accepted:\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\nBilling Approved By:\r\n\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\n\r\nSchick sensor not working in Curve.\r\n\r\nExposure Issue\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\n\r\nRemoved the 3.2 driver and installed the AE USB driver with CDR Twain\r\n\r\nWorking now.\r\n\r\nCurve support stated that they have the new Curve software installed and she did not know about any other software like the integrator.\r\n\r\nHave to call the office back and remove the old driver and install the new driver.\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\nWorking now but with the old driver.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.07.2025          22:48:46            Michael Rosales Jr (DIHDE659)\r\n\r\nAdditional Information\r\n------------------\r\nTransfer to schick\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n18.07.2025          18:58:30            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n\r\nCharlotteNC-Imaging-Escalations@dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.07.2025          18:58:03            Rebecca Buck (RBUCK)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/18/2025 11:57:49 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nCallers Full Name: Ken Mitchel\r\nCallers Phone Number: 970-640-4266\r\nCallers Role: IT\r\n\r\nRemote Access: yes\r\nSidexis Version: 4.4\r\nServer Location:  S4K-GJ-XRAY\r\nPDATA Remote Location: local\r\nPractice Management: Curve\r\nWorkstation(s): S4K-GJ-XRAY\r\nScout Check:\r\n\r\nFirmware: 1.5.140\r\nPlug-in Version: 3.2\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nCurve not seeing new Schick driver.\r\nIT says last tech did not fix issue and Sensor is not working.\r\nThey cannot upgrade to higher Curve and want it to work like before.\r\n\r\nSidexis service not present in 4.4 install.\r\nDownloaded Sidexis to get Sidexis service installed again and install 1.3 twain.\r\nI tested in Tech toolbox twain tester.\r\nI told him he needs to talk with Curve support.\r\nTested in curve with twain.\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\nIT upset and wants to talk with supervisor.\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.07.2025          14:41:48            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n18.07.2025          00:25:50            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\ncurve on call with updated curve capture to connect sensor\r\n__________________\r\nProblem Description\r\n18.07.2025          00:25:50            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/17/2025 5:33:08 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: yes\r\nDealer on-site: no\r\nBillable: NA\r\nBilling Accepted:\r\n\r\n\r\nRemote Access: yes\r\nSidexis Version: NA\r\nServer Location:\r\nPDATA Remote Location:\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable):\r\nPractice Management: Curve Hero\r\nWorkstation(s):\r\nScout Check: yes done\r\n\r\nFirmware: 1.5.121\r\nPlug-in Version:\r\nExposure Count:\r\nUnit IP Address:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description: Sensor connection to Curve hero issue\r\nupdated firmware to 1.5.140 and new IOSS3.2\r\n\r\nneeds curve capture2.32.2 version\r\n\r\ncall dropped was able to call back call choppy\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n17.07.2025          23:34:02            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\nNote\r\n17.07.2025          23:34:02            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
