      "problem_summary": "Sensor connection to Curve hero issue updated firmware to 1.5.140 and new IOSS3.2 needs curve capture2.32.2 version call dropped was able to call back call choppy __________________ Log 17.07.2025 23:34:02 Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ) Note 17.07.2025 23:34:02 Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ) __ Initial ticket creation __ __________________",
      "solution_summary": "for the customer. __________________ ************************Safety Task ************************ Note 05.08.2025 14:21:16 Jen Brown (TRJJB112) Based on the ticket information, there is no injury to the patient or user. The image acquired contains a full previous image or a portion of previous and current image or a blank image which is identifiable. It is not possible for a dentist to provide treatment based on the image acquired and the dentist would need to retake another image to provide treatment. Therefore, there is no risk to the patient for unnecessary treatment and the risk of additional radiation exposure is assessed as part of the product risk management and there are no immediate or long-range consequences. This complaint is evaluated to be Not Reportable within USA and ROW. The issue is being evaluated under CAPA-2024-532. __________________ ************************************************ Log 30.07.2025 00:17:03 Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA) ************************************************ Note 30.07.2025 00:17:03 Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA) From: Stevens, Austin <Austin.Stevens@dentsplysirona.com> Sent: Friday, July 25, 2025 6:45 PM To: kmitchell@sequent-is.com Cc: jakeallen@curvedental.com Mandia, Jeffrey <Jeffrey.Mandia@dentsplysirona.com> Almond, Timothy <Timothy.Almond@dentsplysirona.com> Subject: Re: Curve Integration Hello Ken & Jake, Thanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids. Today we talked about two issues the office is currently facing. 1. Previous patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room 2. Poor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in As discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem. Since this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related. If moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question. Weve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve. The room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in. While discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance. At this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve. The ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361. Thank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer. Warm Regards, Austin Stevens Technical Support Specialist, Imaging __________________ ************************************************ Note 30.07.2025 00:36:18 Jeffrey Mandia (JMANDIA) __ Further Action __ Old patient/New patient image issues and slowness taking images. Schick sensors, 3.0 integration to Curve From: Stevens, Austin <Austin.Stevens@dentsplysirona.com> Sent: Friday, July 25, 2025 6:45 PM To: kmitchell@sequent-is.com Cc: jakeallen@curvedental.com Mandia, Jeffrey <Jeffrey.Mandia@dentsplysirona.com> Almond, Timothy <Timothy.Almond@dentsplysirona.com> Subject: Re: Curve Integration Hello Ken & Jake, Thanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids. Today we talked about two issues the office is currently facing. 1. Previous patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room 2. Poor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in As discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem. Since this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related. If moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question. Weve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve. The room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in. While discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance. At this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve. The ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361. Thank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer. Warm Regards, Austin Stevens Technical Support Specialist, Imaging __________________ Note 29.07.2025 18:09:30 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Further Action __ Tracking number sent to Ken for visibility. __________________ Note 28.07.2025 23:07:21 Carol Cowles (CCOWLES) item shipped Order 3415131 __________________ Note 28.07.2025 21:57:19 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Further Action __ *********** S/N of the affected USB Interface is 2048782. This is not showing up in DSCRM for me to be able to attach to the ticket. *********** __________________ Note 28.07.2025 21:55:22 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Further Action __ Ken reached out and said PTC he had trouble ordering another interface as they werent aware of any issues. Ken says he provided PTC the ticket number as well. - - Sending this to order service for processing. Please send the USB 3.0 interface directly to the practice. - - Thanks! __________________ Note 28.07.2025 18:44:36 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Further Action __ RMA for affected USB interface recommended. They will proceed with the RMA of the USB interface due to old patient / new patient issue. S/N of USB Interface could not be found in DSCRM at the time of the call. __________________ Note 26.07.2025 13:07:12 Austin Stevens (ASTEVENS) __ Further Action __ ------FURTHER ACTION------- 07/26/2025 7:06:32 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time) Called and spoke with Ken from IT and Jake from Curve Dental. See below for email recap: Hello Ken & Jake, Thanks for taking the time to speak with me today about the on going issues with Smiles 4 Kids. Today we talked about two issues the office is currently facing. Previous patients x-rays showing up in a subsequent patients chart in one room Poor x-ray quality and performance using the IOSS (Intra Oral Sensor Software) plug-in As discussed, a firmware update to the USB interface was pushed in an attempt to fix this problem. Since this attempt was unsuccessful the staff will swap the USB interface with another room and test to see if this resolves the first issue since this is linked to being hardware related. If moving the Schick USB interface from another room into this one resolves the issue we create a ticket the office can use to RMA the interface in question. Weve also removed Sidexis version 4.4 from the PC in question as its not needed with the integration of Schick sensors inside of Curve. The room in question is currently using our legacy driver package i.e., Schick AE USB interface driver, and the CDR Intraoral twain originally installed on 07/23 due to reports of poor performance and image quality using the IOSS plug-in. While discussing driver versions I recommended leaving them on that driver suite (for now) due to the aforementioned reports of quality / performance. At this time there is no pre / post x-ray filters that can be applied using the IOSS integration with Curve. The ticket number containing all information for previous calls, and todays is 1263361. Thank you for the continued patience as we work to get this resolved for the customer. Warm Regards, __________________ Note 23.07.2025 18:25:19 Keenan Jordan (KJORDAN) __ Further Action __ ------FURTHER ACTION------- 07/23/2025 11:58:55 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time) Callers Full Name: Ken Mitchell Callers Phone Number: 9706404266 Callers Role: Office IT admin Billing Previously Accepted: Billing Accepted: Billing Approved By: Further Action Issue / Request: Schick sensor not working in Curve. Exposure Issue Troubleshooting Details: Removed the 3.2 driver and installed the AE USB driver with CDR Twain Working now. Curve support stated that they have the new Curve software installed and she did not know about any other software like the integrator. Have to call the office back and remove the old driver and install the new driver. Functional Test Successful / Follow Up: Working now but with the old driver. __________________ Note 18.07.2025 22:48:46 Michael Rosales Jr (DIHDE659) Additional Information ------------------ Transfer to schick __________________ Customer Note 18.07.2025 18:58:30 Rebecca Buck (RBUCK) CharlotteNC-Imaging-Escalations@dentsplysirona.com __________________ Note 18.07.2025 18:58:03 Rebecca Buck (RBUCK) __ Further Action __ ------FURTHER ACTION------- 07/18/2025 11:57:49 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time) Callers Full Name: Ken Mitchel Callers Phone Number: 970-640-4266 Callers Role: IT Remote Access: yes Sidexis Version: 4.4 Server Location: S4K-GJ-XRAY PDATA Remote Location: local Practice Management: Curve Workstation(s): S4K-GJ-XRAY Scout Check: Firmware: 1.5.140 Plug-in Version: 3.2 Troubleshooting Details: Curve not seeing new Schick driver. IT says last tech did not fix issue and Sensor is not working. They cannot upgrade to higher Curve and want it to work like before. Sidexis service not present in 4.4 install. Downloaded Sidexis to get Sidexis service installed again and install 1.3 twain. I tested in Tech toolbox twain tester. I told him he needs to talk with Curve support. Tested in curve with twain. Okay. IT upset and wants to talk with supervisor. Functional Test Successful / Follow Up: __________________ Note 18.07.2025 14:41:48 Jen Brown (TRJJB112) This issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing. These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting. Please close ticket. __________________ Solution Description 18.07.2025 00:25:50 Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ) curve on call with updated curve capture to connect sensor __________________"
