      "description_text": "intermittently not producing xray",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n18.08.2025          13:57:23            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n15.08.2025          09:48:09            Jack Overfield-Recio (DIRTY052)\r\n\r\nHi Eoin,\r\n\r\nIts 12 months on the USB and cable element and 5 on the sensor element. I would recommend raising a claim with bensheim.returnservice@dentsplysirona.com quoting this ticket ref. for clarification or if you wish to claim further.\r\n\r\nThey can also be reached on +49 6251 / 16 - 16 90.\r\n\r\nKind Regards,\r\nJack - DS UK&I\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n15.08.2025          09:37:23             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nHi Jack, what is the warranty on these ? 12 or 24 months ?\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n15.08.2025          09:18:45            Jack Overfield-Recio (DIRTY052)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n15.08.2025          09:18:41            Jack Overfield-Recio (DIRTY052)\r\n\r\nHi Eoin,\r\n\r\nSee feedback from the team in Germany below\r\n\r\nThe sensor is part of kit #6618685 #71017351.\r\nDelivered on October 16, 2023.\r\nThe warranty has expired. The kit was not registered.\r\n\r\nKR,\r\nJack - DS UK&I Digital Support\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n15.08.2025          08:13:51            Thomas Waldraff (DIGSJ847)\r\n\r\nThe sensor is part of kit #6618685 #71017351.\r\nDelivered on October 16, 2023.\r\nThe warranty claim has expired. The kit was not registered.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n14.08.2025          14:40:27            Kirsten Riede (KIRRIE)\r\n\r\nHallo Thomas,\r\nder Sensor ist Bestandteil des Kits #6618685 #71017351\r\nAusgeliefert 16.10.2023\r\nWie du bereits korrekt erkannt hast, ist der Garantieanspruch erloschen. eine Registrierung des Kits hat nicht statt gefunden.\r\n\r\nHilft dir dies bei deiner Anfrage oder sollen wir die Garantieablehnung an den Kunden kommunizieren?\r\n\r\nViele Grüße\r\nKirsten\r\nCustomer Note\r\n13.08.2025          15:06:19             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nhi, any update from benshiesm on this ? customer has just been back on and said theyve troubleshoot the issue and problem is sensoritself and not the box or usb cable.\r\nthanks\r\neoin\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nNote\r\n12.08.2025          07:36:42            Thomas Waldraff (DIGSJ847)\r\n\r\nHallo,\r\n\r\nkönnt ihr schauen wann der Sensor noch Garantie hat.\r\n\r\nEr wurde leider nie Registriert.\r\n\r\nGruß Thomas\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n12.08.2025          07:36:42            Thomas Waldraff (DIGSJ847)\r\n\r\nHallo,\r\n\r\nkönnt ihr schauen wann der Sensor noch Garantie hat.\r\n\r\nEr wurde leider nie Registriert.\r\n\r\nGruß Thomas\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n18.07.2025          20:04:55             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nNumber starting with the 7000 is printed onto the sensor head but the SN on the connector at the lead 64008093.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n18.07.2025          15:16:17             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nit doesnt appear to allow me to edit device serial number but sensor serial number is 70002792\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n18.07.2025          14:06:58            David Balfour (DIKHU013)\r\n\r\nHello Eoin,\r\n\r\nplease provide the serial number of the unit and add to the ticket,\r\ni will then pass to Bensheim to see if the sensor can be replaced under warranty,\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n\r\nDavid Balfour\r\nDigital Support Specialist\r\nField Sales\r\n01453 793190\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDavid.Balfour@dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\nwww.dentsplysirona.com\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n18.07.2025          12:06:24             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nHi,\r\nWe have a customer thats having an intermittent problem with their sensor (havent got serial number to hand but its about 2\r\nyears old). Sometimes when they take an X-ray no image appears and then from time to time it will produce a grey image (will attach\r\nsample). They have tested in another room and issue has reoccurred there also. They have also asked us if normal for the led light o\r\nn the control module (computer icon ) to go from bright to dim? I will attached video.\r\nThanks\r\nEoin\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n18.07.2025          12:06:23             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nHi,\r\nWe have a customer thats having an intermittent problem with their sensor (havent got serial number to hand but its about 2\r\nyears old). Sometimes when they take an X-ray no image appears and then from time to time it will produce a grey image (will attach\r\nsample). They have tested in another room and issue has reoccurred there also. They have also asked us if normal for the led light o\r\nn the control module (computer icon ) to go from bright to dim? I will attached video.\r\nThanks\r\nEoin\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n18.07.2025          12:06:23             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
