      "notes_text": "Note\r\n21.07.2025          14:29:57            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and it was determined that a part of the system must be replaced.\r\nReplacement part has been recommended.  Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n18.07.2025          21:17:59            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/18/2025 2:33:23 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: Yes\r\nDealer on-site: No\r\nBillable: No\r\n\r\nRemote Access: Yes\r\nSidexis Version: N/A\r\nPractice Management: Open Dental\r\nWorkstation(s): OP2\r\nScout Check: Yes\r\n\r\nFirmware: USB 1.4.107 to 1.5.140\r\nPlug-in Version:\r\nExposure Count:\r\nUnit IP Address:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\nThere is a USB box that is failing to be detected even when the PC shows something is detected\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n18.07.2025          21:17:59            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\nSolution Description:\r\nConnected to the OP2 and found they are still using the 5.16 and CDR twain options for Open Dental capture\r\nThe USB is not detected at all SN: 2011298\r\nthey connected a spare USB and it is automatically detected, noticed Firmware is still on v. 1.4.107 so we updated\r\n\r\nthe USB will need to be replaced\r\n\r\nThey have another USB box with the same issue and as she was swapping out the USB boxes she also tried between 3 different ports of the PC\r\nthey were connected but not detected each time -- she then mentioned that the working USB that worked a moment ago is now undetected\r\n\r\nadvised to have the USB ports check that if they are providing proper power 25045797\r\nIT stated this is NOT the issue since they are new PCs and he confirmed they are providing the correct Voltage\r\nWhen I asked for the reading and should have reading of 5v (min 4.9v) -- he did not check reading\r\n\r\nthis is also when staff mentioned Power surge error message reported on other PCs as well related to power surge and not provided\r\nIT is now walking her through using an external USB extension cable to test...did not advise so we had her use another USB cable to eliminate cables\r\nStill, none of the USB boxes are being detected, even the one that worked earlier -- USB needs more power message reported (screenshot attached)\r\n\r\nIT then found out office experienced a power outage when entire office lost power and PCs were shut down unexpectedly\r\nIT and his team will be on-site with their tools to diagnose if the PC is the issue and if USB is determined to be the issue they will order USB (notepad left on desktop)\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): No\r\nThe USB that is working on 1 PC will remain left alone so as to maintain the ability to capture from that PC\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n18.07.2025          20:40:13            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\nNote\r\n18.07.2025          20:40:13            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
