      "description_text": "intermittent failure",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n28.07.2025          19:10:47            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nIt cannot be determined from the information provided if this issue is software or hardware related.  It will be kept as a service ticket unless additional information can be provided by the customer.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n22.07.2025          15:35:42            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n22.07.2025          15:35:41            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nIntermittent connections like this can be due to faulty USB cables, broken connectors on the Schick USB module, or sometimes even inadequate power delivery from the computer. We would need some additional information to troubleshoot this more thoroughly I would suggest calling our main support line:\r\n\r\n1-800-659-5977 (Opt. 3 for End User Support > Opt. 2 for Imaging)\r\n\r\nClosing ticket for now we can reopen later for further troubleshooting, if needed.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n21.07.2025          19:49:41             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nnot working (intermittent) the light turn on sometimes when plug it\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n21.07.2025          19:49:40             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nnot working (intermittent) the light turn on sometimes when plug it\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n21.07.2025          19:49:40             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
