      "category_level_4": "Black or white image",
      "firmware": "",
      "support_hub": "US",
      "description_text": "black image after aquire",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n22.07.2025          20:14:50            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n22.07.2025          16:47:52             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nThank you. I think I have it resolved now as there seemed to be a few things causing it. Firmware was all up to date as well as I  ran the module and sensor test on the AE upgrade app. IT has some user rights blocking on that user profile, also customer replacedthe cable themselves. I took cable apart, cleaned both with alcohol and put back, I could then see the sensor. Power cycled module  from PC and all seemed to work. I think the black was just a very zoomed in shot from Twack, as when tested in Romexis via twain  the sensor now works in multiple ops. Customer has put back in circulation and will update ticket if fails to connect again.  Thanks.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n22.07.2025          15:59:51            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nPlease refer to customer communication via Customer Notes\r\n__________________\r\nCustomer Note\r\n22.07.2025          15:59:50            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nI would first suggest double checking that the firmware on the sensor and the USB module are up to date, as there were some image processing improvements made in newer versions. If that has already been done, this could be a defective sensor and we could replace it once were able to verify warranty status of the sensor itself.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n21.07.2025          21:29:21             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nSchick33 size 2 sn# 25070810 acquiring black images. sensor is new, swapped cables same issue.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n21.07.2025          21:29:20             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nSchick33 size 2 sn# 25070810 acquiring black images. sensor is new, swapped cables same issue.\r\n\r\n+++\r\n+++\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n21.07.2025          21:29:20             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)",
