      "description_text": "new schick sensor integration",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n23.07.2025          13:59:15            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n22.07.2025          17:58:19            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/22/2025 10:41:00 AM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: NA\r\nDealer on-site: YES\r\nBillable: NO\r\nBilling Accepted: No\r\nDetails: Inquiry\r\n\r\nFollow Up:\r\n\r\nDealer tech needed assistance setting up Schick legacy drivers/CDR Twain for use with Tracker\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n22.07.2025          17:58:19            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n\r\nLogged into SACSM-D04004 and downloaded/installed prereqs with toolbox, (.NET 3.5 failed twice for some reason, took a while) as well as Schick AE USB driver 1.1, CDR Twain, MSXML Parser and CDR Patch 2808 for 13th gen CPU, disabled Core isolation.\r\n\r\nTested via TWAIN tester in Tech Toolbox and after plugging it into the rear USB port for better power delivery, it was working as expected. test shot went through fine. left all the drivers and installers in a numbered list in a main folder for the tech to use elsewhere if needed.\r\n__________________\r\nNote\r\n22.07.2025          16:41:04            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\n\r\nLog\r\n22.07.2025          16:41:03            Taylor Bledsoe (DIIDF904)",
