provided by Attila Csekes:\r\nDear Support,\r\n\r\n\r\nplease mark this ticket as CAPA related. We are experiencing the same issue as in ticket 8001242831.\r\n\r\n\r\nThank you very much!\r\nBR\r\nAttila Csekes\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n18.08.2025          15:13:28            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has previously been identified and is being investigated under CAPA 2024-532.  Further evaluation of individual complaints will be conducted as required. Complaints are monitored for trend monthly for the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close complaint upon appropriate resolution for the customer.\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n17.08.2025          09:37:34             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nHi, This customer is still using Onepix software as reported before, no SIDEXIS 4 logs available then. I will check for S/N.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n12.08.2025          08:22:49            Thomas Waldraff (DIGSJ847)\r\n\r\nHallo,\r\n\r\nplease send us\r\n\r\nthe serial number of the sensor\r\nthe serial number of the USB BOX\r\n\r\nDevice LOG file\r\n\r\nDetailed description of the offending image quality, draw in errors\r\n\r\nNGLogCollect Clientstation and Sidexis4Service\r\n\r\nEvent display applications and system\r\n\r\nExport of 2 - 3 images via DICOM\r\n\r\nCorresponding data containers\r\n\r\nBr Thomas\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nCustomer Note\r\n24.07.2025          08:20:42             CPIC_SIMO (CPIC_SIMO)\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nSame problem on a new clinic in Östergötland.\r\n\r\nThe description is that the pixeled image is from a previous patient, not the pa\r\ntient before, it was even before that patient. This images comes when they try to take a new image on a new patient. The IT technici\r\nan also question how this comes and if this is also related to the retrieve last image function that is not implemented in Onepix?\r\n\r\n\r\nBest Regards\r\n\r\nJohan\r\n\r\n+++\r\n