      "description_text": "twain errors | usb firmware updatae",
      "notes_text": "Note\r\n04.08.2025          21:29:27            Armando Santacruz (ASANTACRUZ)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\nclosing ticket per J. Brown\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n04.08.2025          17:54:10            Jen Brown (TRJJB112)\r\n\r\nThis issue has been troubleshooted and was determined to be related to software or connectivity related within the office and is considered routine servicing.  These requests are monitored for trend monthly at the Product Surveillance Committee (PSC) meeting.\r\n\r\nPlease close ticket.\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nNote\r\n28.07.2025          18:34:24            Andy Goodman (AGOODMAN)\r\n\r\n__  Further Action __\r\n------FURTHER ACTION-------  07/28/2025 12:11:10 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\nCallers Full Name:  Alex Meddings\r\nCallers Phone Number:  8565818770\r\nCallers Role:  IT\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nWarranty:  Yes\r\nDealer Technician on-site:  No\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nRemote Access:\r\nSidexis Version:\r\nServer Location:\r\nPDATA Remote Location:\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable):\r\nPractice Management:\r\nWorkstation(s):\r\nScout Check:\r\n\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nFirmware:\r\nPlug-in Version:\r\nExposure Count:\r\nUnit IP Address:\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nFurther Action Issue / Request:\r\nSchick Install with IOSS3.2\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nTroubleshooting Details:\r\nIT requested to have the Schick sensors installed for use within DTX\r\nI installed and tested TWAIN on OP02 - worked perfect\r\nNeed to install on SERVER01\r\nInstalled Sidexis on the server - needs a reboot\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\nFunctional Test Successful / Follow Up:\r\nIT will contact us to finalize install when the server can be rebooted\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nProblem Description\r\n24.07.2025          22:40:31            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n--------INITIAL LOG-------- 07/24/2025 4:18:46 PM (Dentsply Sirona Charlotte Time)\r\n\r\nWarranty: Yes\r\nDealer on-site: No\r\nBillable: No\r\n\r\nRemote Access: yes\r\nSidexis Version: N/A\r\nServer Location:\r\nPDATA Remote Location:\r\nRCU Location (If Applicable):\r\nPractice Management: DTX Studio\r\nWorkstation(s): OP04\r\nScout Check: yes\r\n\r\nFirmware: USB v. 1.5.121 to 1.5.14\r\nPlug-in Version:\r\nExposure Count:\r\nUnit IP Address:\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting Description:\r\nTwain capture reporting errors and they cant capture\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nSolution Description\r\n24.07.2025          22:40:31            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\nSolution Description:\r\nConnected to OP04 and found they are using the older drivers with CDR twain\r\nthe firmware on USB is still on v. 1.5.121\r\n\r\nhe contacted office to have them disconnect sensor -- updated firmware on USB box\r\nallowed them to test all things on our end working fine: allows them to setup for exposure and shows sensor is ready for exposure\r\n\r\nnot exposure can be taken. They reached out to DTX studio and were told to contact us. I explained our driver functions and that they are allowing them to get to the point to take exposure. Also advised them to check the device that is pushing radiation -- hes not sure of their device but I provided them the technique factor sheet\r\n\r\n\r\nFunctional (Yes/No): yes as far as our drivers and plug-ins\r\n\r\n\r\n__________________\r\n\r\nLog\r\n24.07.2025          22:20:21            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\nNote\r\n24.07.2025          22:20:21            Talia Nastacio (TNASTACIO)\r\n\r\n__ Initial ticket creation __\r\n\r\n__________________",
      "excel_matched": true,
      "desc_primary_raw": "Software/Firmware/Driver",
      "desc_secondary_raw": "Firmware",
